    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** emerges as our highest-scoring asset at 65.32, bolstered by a prime spot in the order against Sonny Gray. While Gray typically presents a challenge, the projected wind conditions provide a 10% lift that, when combined with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2019s favorable platoon split, makes him our anchor for the day. Close behind, **Gunnar Henderson** (62.18) remains a high-floor start despite facing an elite arm in Bryan Woo; his dynamic platoon edge and second-order placement mitigate the risk posed by Woo\u2019s xERA. **Jacob Wilson** (60.70) and **Drake Baldwin** (60.64) round out our top-tier plays, both benefiting from high-leverage lineup slots that maximize their scoring potential in what should be favorable hitting environments.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal gap between **Sam Antonacci** (43.29) and **Josh Jung** (42.87) on the bench. While **Josh Jung**\u2019s talent profile is high, he was edged out by **Sam Antonacci** due to the latter\u2019s extreme situational utility; despite facing a lefty, the 10% wind benefit and **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s ability to maximize speed-based points in a SB-starved league kept him in the lineup. Conversely, we are keeping **Brayan Rocchio** (41.40) active, though he remains a marginal play as he faces a tough matchup against a lefty pitcher (xERA 3.32) that severely limits his ceiling. Managers should keep a close eye on the official lineups for **Drake Baldwin**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Sam Antonacci**, as any shifts down the order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their efficiency scores. Finally, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL, as we look for ways to optimize our stolen base production elsewhere.",
